  "actualTrackingIssueBody": "## Outcome\n\n**F123 is measured no-gain, not a performance PR.** Three complete source comparisons retain 1,152 observations. The declared copied-five IndexOf primary has paired less-time effects -56.51% / -53.66% / 81.23%; negative means slower. Median: 53.66% more time, 0 B/op reported in both sources. Every favorable/adverse/first-hit/last-hit and unchanged Contains outcome remains; the timing budget is permanently closed.\n\n## Connected artifacts\n\n| Artifact | Link |\n|---|---|\n| Immutable evidence and limits | https://github.com/jaslawinMs/aspnetcore/blob/677f26a9fe342f2969f7a0ca912d945bd59ace1f/F123/README.md |\n| Diagnostic source experiment; not recommended for merge | https://github.com/jaslawinMs/aspnetcore/commit/8f72875eb6c2a108e529b93714dd56e3d8e0c154 |\n| Twelve focused preservation rows | https://github.com/jaslawinMs/aspnetcore/blob/8f72875eb6c2a108e529b93714dd56e3d8e0c154/src/Mvc/Mvc.Core/test/Infrastructure/CopyOnWriteListTest.cs |\n| Runnable exact-eight-input BDN project | https://github.com/jaslawinMs/aspnetcore/blob/677f26a9fe342f2969f7a0ca912d945bd59ace1f/F123/harness/AutoPerf.Benchmarks.csproj |\n| Every measurement, control and variability table | https://github.com/jaslawinMs/aspnetcore/blob/677f26a9fe342f2969f7a0ca912d945bd59ace1f/F123/comparison-results.md |\n| Requirement coverage, exact commands and outcomes | https://github.com/jaslawinMs/aspnetcore/blob/677f26a9fe342f2969f7a0ca912d945bd59ace1f/F123/validation-commands.md |\n| Actual independent eight-input rebuild | https://github.com/jaslawinMs/aspnetcore/blob/677f26a9fe342f2969f7a0ca912d945bd59ace1f/F123/reconstruction-paired-001/verified-reproduction.json |\n| Full audit: 117 accepted XML executions, 22 runtime / 288 settings records | https://github.com/jaslawinMs/aspnetcore/blob/677f26a9fe342f2969f7a0ca912d945bd59ace1f/F123/audit-summary.json |\n| Permanently closed budget | https://github.com/jaslawinMs/aspnetcore/blob/677f26a9fe342f2969f7a0ca912d945bd59ace1f/F123/permanent-budget-close.json |\n\nThe actual default and original pass the same faithful boundary. The action itself executes public IList.IndexOf and its result is verified over HTTP. That proves optional consumer reachability, not ordinary framework frequency. Object.Equals, reference/value-type typed-equality differences, first match, order, mutation/version semantics and arbitrary-source disposal remain green on both sources.\n\nAn initial Moq-private-type preparation failure and a subsequent report-routing mistake are retained and explicitly disclosed; the initial failing TRX was overwritten, not preserved. The fresh accepted original/candidate XML rows all reach their assertions and pass. No shipping semantic bug is claimed.\n\nNo primary retargeting, more timing, performance PR/browser launch, application-throughput, specific JIT-cause, compiled-page/browser or merge-readiness claim. Fixed classified report unchanged.\n\n\n**Retained third-pair shift:** Original primary means are 10.70 / 10.73 / 90.39 ns; candidate means are 16.75 / 16.48 / 16.97 ns. The +81.23% third-pair effect is retained alongside the two adverse effects, not treated as a repeatable improvement or assigned a specific cause. The declared median, two-of-three timing and allocation gates do not pass.\n\nThe immutable evidence snapshot predates its additive [verified publication receipt](https://github.com/jaslawinMs/aspnetcore/blob/autoperf-results/F123/publication.json). All 1406 sealed files remain pinned and unchanged. The third Original primary has two retained spikes, 162.39% CV and an 11.01 ns median; its 90.39 ns mean is not a stable throughput result. No performance PR is warranted; the independent source branch is retained only as a no-gain experiment.\n",
